      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.1 Advent of British Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The British East India Company gradually extended control over Rajputana (then called Rajputana). By 1818, almost all Rajput states had signed subsidiary alliance treaties with the British. The British Resident was stationed at Ajmer, which was directly under British control.",
      "id": "5uhezai"
    },
    {
      "id": "3v0xr7d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.2 Revolt of 1857 in Rajasthan"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The 1857 Revolt affected Rajasthan, but most Rajput rulers remained loyal to the British due to treaty obligations. Important events:",
      "id": "ch3t5jc"
